 "interpretation": "REAL dashcam footage (CCD official test, 900 clips, prevalence 0.076). Registered G1+G2 PASS: frozen DINOv2 AUC-PR 0.561 vs scratch CNN 0.206 and pixel probe 0.205 (diff vs CNN +0.354, video-cluster CI95 [0.311,0.397]); realized FPR 0.023 <= 0.10. The registered SOURCE-CONFOUND CONTROL is the key reading: overall ROC is high for every model (0.80-0.95) because crash clips (YouTube) and normal clips (BDD100K) differ in source/style. Within crash clips only, which removes that confound, the scratch CNN (ROC 0.518) and pixel probe (0.501) are at CHANCE: their apparent skill is source discrimination, not anticipation. The frozen pretrained encoders keep real within-clip anticipation (DINOv2 0.774, MobileNetV2 0.769). At the 5% calibration the pretrained models warn before onset on 71-77% of crash clips with a mean lead of ~1.5 s while alarming on 0.2% of normal clips; the headline numbers are still inflated by the source confound, and within-clip ROC ~0.77 is the honest anticipation measure. Pretraining matters far more on real footage (+0.354 AUC-PR) than in the sim (+0.018). This validates the approach on real video in a DIFFERENT domain; it does not qualify the sim advisory head (vision_caution_integration_protocol_v1.json)."
